# Runtime pins for the inference-complete LMRS image (C-059).
#
# These live in version control, not in .env, because they are part of what the
# image IS, not a credential: a released image tag must be reproducible from the
# commit it was built from. .env and the environment still override them for a
# one-off experiment.
#
# Chosen 2026-07-30 as the newest stable pair that can actually work together:
#
#   LMCache 0.5.2 is the latest stable release (2026-07-22).
#   vLLM 0.25.1 is the latest vLLM that existed when it shipped (2026-07-14).
#
# vLLM 0.26.0 was released 2026-07-25, three days AFTER LMCache 0.5.2, so no
# LMCache release has been built or tested against it. LMCache plugs into vLLM
# through the KV connector interface (LMCacheConnectorV1, passed by
# docker-entrypoint.sh via --kv-transfer-config), which is coupled to vLLM
# internals and changes across minors, so pairing them is how the connector
# breaks at run time rather than at build time.
#
# When a newer LMCache appears, raise both pins together and confirm the
# connector loads before releasing: the pairing rule is "LMCache first, then the
# newest vLLM that predates it", not "newest of each".

LMRS_VLLM_BASE=vllm/vllm-openai:v0.25.1
LMRS_LMCACHE_VERSION=0.5.2
